  "construction": "Halving of the weight-6 cyclic two-block code [[510,16,26]] (codes/510-16-26.json) along a fixed-point-free ZX-duality that swaps the two blocks (symplectic halving: Lee, Okada, Maskara, Kasai, Zhou, arXiv:2609.30069, Def. 3; Burton, Durso-Sabina, Brown, arXiv:2406.09951, Thm. 3.5). Parent: G = Z/255; qubit (1,h) -> h, (2,h) -> 255+h; X-check g on (1, g+F_A) and (2, g+F_B), Z-check g on (1, g-F_B) and (2, g-F_A), F_A = {0,26,76}, F_B = {0,30,66} (a = 1+x^26+x^76, b = 1+x^30+x^66; equal to codes/510-16-26.json). Involution: Psi(1,h) = (2, 15 + 154h), Psi(2,h) = (1, 154(h - 15)) mod 255 (154^2 = 1 mod 255). Fold: fold qubit h is the pair {(1,h), Psi(1,h)}; the X-check a gives the generator with X on {h : (1,h) in a} and Z on {h : Psi(1,h) in a}, in the order of the X-checks. n = 255, rank 247, k = 8; 204 generators of weight 6 and 51 of weight 5 with one Y each; not locally Clifford equivalent to a CSS code.",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "arXiv:2406.09951",
   "arXiv:1904.02703"
  ],
  "date": "2026-11-10",
  "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
  "notes": "16 <= d <= 22. Lower bound, proved (computer-assisted): a nontrivial logical p with y Y factors and t X or Z factors corresponds to a nontrivial Z-logical of the parent of weight 2y + t; t is even since the parent's column weights are odd, so the Pauli weight y + t is at least (26 + t)/2, using d = 26 for 510-16-26 (Theorem 4.1 of weight6-exact-distances/exact_distances.pdf, github.com/TimoKellerMath/quantum-error-correction @ 2be467a7bd36); an exhaustive search over the logicals with t <= 4 gives the least weights 81, 59, 36 for t = 0, 2, 4 and none for t = 1, 3, hence d >= 16. Upper bound: the witness, one of 102 logicals of weight 22 found (two orbits of size 51 under an automorphism group of order 102); 3e6 information-set trials (random qubit order in random single-qubit Clifford frames, and random order of the symplectic coordinates) found nothing lighter, and exact orbit folds exclude invariant logicals of weight <= 24 under the rotation subgroups; d = 22 is not proved. Programs, data and logs: github.com/TimoKellerMath/quantum-error-correction @ c203901854da, amplified-and-folded-codes/. New on the stabilizer board: no entry with these n and k, and no stabilizer entry dominates even [[255,8,16]]; across code types, CSS entries such as 240-8-20-b ([[240,8,20]], check weight 6) would dominate it if d <= 20. Not locally Clifford equivalent to a CSS code (51 qubits carry X, Y and Z among the generators); checked, not equivalent to an existing entry."
